  "notes": "{用意|ようい} means preparation, with emphasis on having things ready and at hand. It is used both as a noun and as a する verb.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- No standard intransitive pair\n- Pattern: [noun]⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{用意|ようい}する\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {用意|ようい}する: to prepare (something)\n- {用意|ようい}ができる: to be ready, preparations are done\n- 〜の{用意|ようい}: preparation for ~\n- {用意|ようい}⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦いい→いい：00118_ii⟧: well-prepared, resourceful\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{準備|じゅんび}→準備：01431_junbi⟧: preparation (broader scope, more formal)\n- ⟦{支度|したく}→支度：02083_shitaku⟧: preparation (specifically getting ready to go out, getting dressed)\n- {用意|ようい}: preparation (having items or arrangements ready)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {用意|ようい}、⟦スタート→スタート：11053_sutaato⟧！: Ready, set, go!\n- ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧{用意|ようい}: mental preparation\n- ご{用意|ようい}ください: please prepare/have ready (polite)",
